  "style": {
    "id": "loom-weave",
    "name": "Loom Weave",
    "description": "A wooden tabletop jacquard loom in bright daylight, seen from the weaver's side: cream warp threads, a harness of string heddles that lift threads one by one, a boat shuttle flying red, gold and blue weft through the shed, a reed beating each row into the fell, and the growing cloth rendered crossing by crossing (a shader reads the weave draft: over/under per crossing, thread relief and twist). Beside the cloth a brown punched card glows on a lightbox and advances one row per pick in step with the cloth, so each row of holes sits beside the row of cloth it wove. A draft planner (pattern bitmap + plain-weave borders) decides every lift; shed, shuttle, beat, cloth advance, card pins and every clack, swish and thump are functions of t from the same pick plan, which speeds up so a motif emerges out of ordinary-looking rows.",
